r>\n   261→\n   262→    <div class=\"container\">\n   263→        <div class=\"main-content\">\n   264→            <!-- New Products Section (40% width) -->\n   265→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   266→                <h2>New Products</h2>\n   267→\n   268→                <div class=\"item\">\n   269→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   270→                        <a href=\"https://superset.sh\" target=\"_blank\">Superset</a>\n   271→                        <span class=\"source-badge source-yc\">YC P26</span>\n   272→                    </div>\n   273→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   274→                        Agent-native IDE that orchestrates multiple AI coding agents in parallel, using git worktree isolation to prevent conflicts. Supports Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Cursor Agent, and other CLI-based coding agents. Features remote workspaces to run agents on other machines.\n   275→                    </div>\n   276→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   277→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   278→                        <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n   279→                        <span class=\"tag\">Git Worktree</span>\n   280→                        <a href=\"https://superset.sh\" target=\"_blank\">superset.sh</a>\n   281→                    </div>\n   282→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Not an agent, but an OS for running agents\"</div>\n   283→                </div>\n   284→\n   285→                <div class=\"item\">\n   286→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   287→                        <a href=\"https://antigravity.google\" target=\"_blank\">Google Antigravity CLI</a>\n   288→                        <span class=\"source-badge source-ph\">#2 PH</span>\n   289→                    </div>\n   290→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   291→                        Terminal-based coding agent CLI for running and monitoring AI coding agents directly from command line. Features multi-step reasoning, multi-file editing, tool calling, and persistent history. Designed for SSH sessions and keyboard-focused workflows.\n   292→                    </div>\n   293→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   294→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI CLI</span>\n   295→                        <span class=\"tag\">SSH</span>\n   296→                        <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n   297→                        <a href=\"https://antigravity.google\" target=\"_blank\">antigravity.google</a>\n   298→                    </div>\n   299→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Most lightweight way to invoke, monitor, and interact with Antigravity agents\"</div>\n   300→                </div>\n   301→\n   302→                <div class=\"item\">\n   303→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   304→                        <a href=\"https://antigravity.google\" target=\"_blank\">Google Antigravity 2.0</a>\n   305→                        <span class=\"source-badge source-tech\">Google I/O</span>\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   308→                        Google's agent-first IDE launched at I/O 2026, featuring standalone desktop application and CLI tool. Centralized workspace to steer, customize, and orchestrate coding agents with memory efficiency breakthroughs and expanded context management.\n   309→                    </div>\n   310→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   311→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   312→                        <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n   313→                        <span class=\"tag\">Workspace</span>\n   314→                        <a href=\"https://antigravity.google\" target=\"_blank\">antigravity.google</a>\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"First major step towards independent AI development environment\"</div>\n   317→                </div>\n   318→            </section>\n   319→\n   320→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35% width) -->\n   321→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   322→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   323→\n   324→                <div class=\"item\">\n   325→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   326→                        <a href=\"https://claude.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code v2.1.156</a>\n   327→                        <span class=\"update-type update-feature\">feature</span>\n   328→                    </div>\n   329→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   330→                        Opus 4.8 Launch and Dynamic Workflows. Released Claude Opus 4.8 with improved performance and accuracy. Introduced dynamic workflows that adapt to task complexity. Enhanced terminal interaction with better command suggestions.\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   333→                        <span>2026-05-29</span>\n   334→                        <a href=\"https://claude.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">changelog</a>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Coding in 2026 hits differently - gave a Figma screenshot and had Claude generate the corresponding screen in existing codebase\"</div>\n   337→                </div>\n   338→\n   339→                <div class=\"item\">\n   340→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   341→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf v2.3.15</a>\n   342→                        <span class=\"update-type update-feature\">feature</span>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   345→                        Devin Local Agent and Claude Opus 4.8. Updated Devin Local agent with improved context handling. Added support for Claude Opus 4.8 model. Enhanced Cascade prediction features and improved file navigation.\n   346→                    </div>\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   348→                        <span>2026-05-28</span>\n   349→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">changelog</a>\n   350→                    </div>\n   351→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Windsurf has better support for hooks than Cursor and full MCP support\"</div>\n   352→                </div>\n   353→\n   354→                <div class=\"item\">\n   355→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   356→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a>\n   357→                        <span class=\"update-type update-feature\">feature</span>\n   358→                    </div>\n   359→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   360→                        Automations and /loop Skill. Introduced Cursor Automations for recurring development tasks. Added /loop skill for iterative code improvement. Implemented shared canvases for team collaboration.\n   361→                    </div>\n   362→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   363→                        <span>2026-05-26</span>\n   364→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">changelog</a>\n   365→                    </div>\n   366→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Multiple Cursor meetups and hackathons organized across Europe, Asia, and other regions in May 2026\"</div>\n   367→                </div>\n   368→\n   369→                <div class=\"item\">\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   371→                        <a href=\"https://continue.dev/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v0.8.12</a>\n   372→                        <span class=\"update-type update-bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   375→                        Context Window Improvements. Improved context window handling for better code comprehension. Added support for additional model providers. Fixed issues with VS Code integration.\n   376→                    </div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   378→                        <span>2026-05-24</span>\n   379→                        <a href=\"https://continue.dev/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">changelog</a>\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→                </div>\n   382→\n   383→                <div class=\"item\">\n   384→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   385→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n   386→                        <span class=\"update-type update-feature\">feature</span>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   389→                        Model Updates and Memory Controls. Updated underlying models on May 20, 2026. Introduced memory controls allowing users to manage what context Copilot retains. Enhanced agent sessions with better multi-step reasoning.\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   392→                        <span>2026-05-20</span>\n   393→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">changelog</a>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"2021-2026, Goodbye, Copilot. But with Copilot shifting to usage-based billing, it's time to say goodbye\"</div>\n   396→                </div>\n   397→            </section>\n   398→\n   399→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25% width) -->\n   400→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   401→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   402→\n   403→                <div class=\"item\">\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   405→                        <a href=\"https://claude.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Opus 4.8 Launch</a>\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   408→                        Anthropic released Opus 4.8 with dynamic workflows adapting to task complexity. Enhanced terminal interaction with better command suggestions. Strong positive reception with examples of generating UI from Figma screenshots.\n   409→                    </div>\n   410→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   411→                        <div>By: Anthropic / Claude Team</div>\n   412→                        <div>Source: TechMedia | 2026-05-29</div>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   415→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n   416→                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude</span>\n   417→                        <span class=\"tag\">Agentic</span>\n   418→                    </div>\n   419→                </div>\n   420→\n   421→                <div class=\"item\">\n   422→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   423→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf 2.3.15 Integration</a>\n   424→                    </div>\n   425→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   426→                        Windsurf updated with improved Devin Local agent context handling and Claude Opus 4.8 support. Enhanced Cascade prediction features. Superior hooks support and full MCP support compared to Cursor.\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   429→                        <div>By: Windsurf / Codeium</div>\n   430→                        <div>Source: TechMedia | 2026-05-28</div>\n   431→                    </div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   433→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   434→                        <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n   435→                        <span class=\"tag\">Devin</span>\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                </div>\n   438→\n   439→                <div class=\"item\">\n   440→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   441→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor Automations Launch</a>\n   442→                    </div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   444→                        Cursor introduced Automations for recurring development tasks and /loop skill for iterative code improvement. Shared canvases for team collaboration. 50% discount on agent runs for new automations.\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   447→                        <div>By: Cursor Team</div>\n   448→                        <div>Source: TechMedia | 2026-05-26</div>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   451→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   452→                        <span class=\"tag\">Automations</span>\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                </div>\n   455→\n   456→                <div class=\"item\">\n   457→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   458→                        <a href=\"https://superset.sh\" target=\"_blank\">Superset: Multi-Agent IDE</a>\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   461→                        Agent-native IDE orchestrating multiple AI coding agents in parallel using git worktree isolation. Core innovation is multi-agent orchestration engine. YC P26 batch project with 11k+ GitHub stars.\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   464→                        <div>By: Superset Team / YC</div>\n   465→                        <div>Source: HN | 2026-05-23</div>\n   466→                    </div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   468→                        <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n   469→                        <span class=\"tag\">YC</span>\n   470→                        <span class=\"tag\">Git</span>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                </div>\n   473→\n   474→                <div class=\"item\">\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   476→                        <a href=\"https://antigravity.google\" target=\"_blank\">Google Antigravity CLI</a>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   479→                        Google released terminal-based coding agent for command line workflows. Multi-step reasoning, multi-file editing, tool calling, and persistent history. Ranked #2 on Product Hunt. Designed for SSH sessions.\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   482→                        <div>By: Google / Antigravity Team</div>\n   483→                        <div>Source: TechMedia | 2026-05-23</div>\n   484→                    </div>\n   485→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   486→                        <span class=\"tag\">CLI</span>\n   487→                        <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n   488→                        <span class=\"tag\">SSH</span>\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                </div>\n   491→            </section>\n   492→        </div>\n   493→    </div>\n   494→\n   495→    <footer>\n   496→        <p>Report generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK</p>\n   497→        <p style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">\n   498→            <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n   499→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> |\n   500→            <a href=\"#\">Methodology</a> |\n   501→            <a href=\"#\">Conta